#### Chapter 4 Extension Pack Configuration

###### Redfish Expansion Pack Configuration
```
- git clone https://git.ami.com/core/ami-bmc/one-tree/ami/amipacks/redfish meta-ami/recipes-ami/redfish
- Enable Packages for Redfish

    Add EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES:append = " onetree-rtp" in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample

    When we download above URL , it will automatically starts building redfish expansion packs
    bmcweb append file itself will build redfish expansion packs. 
```

###### BRCM RAID Management Expansion Pack Configuration
```
- git clone https://git.ami.com/core/ami-bmc/one-tree/ami/amipacks/raid/raid-brcm meta-ami/recipes-ami/raid-brcm
- git clone https://git.ami.com/core/ami-bmc/one-tree/ami/amipacks/raid/storage meta-ami/recipes-ami/storage
- Enable Packages for BRCM RAID
    a.  Build for ast2600evb 
        a-1. Enable RAID and HBA features:
            Add EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES:append = " onetree-brcmraid" in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample
        a-2. Set I2C OOB mode
            Kindly refer to "MegaRAC OneTree - BRCM RAID Management Expansion Pack Getting Started Guide", Chapter Config OOB (Out of Band) Interface 
    b.  Build for Other CRBs
        b-1. Enable RAID and HBA features:
            Add EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES:append = " onetree-brcmraid onetree-brcmraid8" in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample
```

###### MSCC RAID Management Expansion Pack Configuration
```
- git clone https://git.ami.com/core/ami-bmc/one-tree/ami/amipacks/raid/raid-mscc meta-ami/recipes-ami/raid-mscc
- git clone https://git.ami.com/core/ami-bmc/one-tree/ami/amipacks/raid/storage meta-ami/recipes-ami/storage
- Enable Packages for MSCC RAID

    Add EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES:append = " onetree-msccraid" in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample
```

###### Intel ACD Expansion Pack Configuration
```
- git clone https://git.ami.com/core/ami-bmc/one-tree/intel/meta-restricted meta-core/meta-restricted
- Add meta-restricted layer into “meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/bblayers.conf.sample” 

    BBLAYERS ?= " \
    :
    ##OEROOT##/meta-core/meta-bhs \
    ##OEROOT##/meta-core/meta-intel \
    ##OEROOT##/meta-core/meta-restricted \  <== Added
    :
- Enable Packages for Intel ACD

    Add EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES:append = " onetree-acd" in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample
    Add EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES:append = " onetree-asd" in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample
```

###### Intel ASD Expansion Pack Configuration
```
- git clone https://git.ami.com/core/ami-bmc/one-tree/intel/meta-restricted meta-core/meta-restricted
- Add meta-restricted layer into “meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/bblayers.conf.sample” 

    BBLAYERS ?= " \
    :
    ##OEROOT##/meta-core/meta-bhs \
    ##OEROOT##/meta-core/meta-intel \
    ##OEROOT##/meta-core/meta-restricted \  <== Added 
    :
- Enable Packages for Intel ASD

    Add EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES:append = " onetree-asd" in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample
```

###### Intel MRT Expansion Pack Configuration
```
- git clone https://git.ami.com/core/ami-bmc/one-tree/intel/meta-restricted meta-core/meta-restricted
- Add meta-restricted layer into “meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/bblayers.conf.sample” 

    BBLAYERS ?= " \
    :
    ##OEROOT##/meta-core/meta-bhs \
    ##OEROOT##/meta-core/meta-intel \
    ##OEROOT##/meta-core/meta-restricted \  <== Added
    :
- Enable Packages for Intel MRT

    Add those configurations as below in ./meta-core/meta-restricted/conf/layer.conf 

    Add EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES:append = " onetree-mrt" in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample

- Enable Redfish Expansion Pack
```

###### Intel PFR Expansion Pack Configuration
```
- git clone https://git.ami.com/core/ami-bmc/one-tree/intel/meta-restricted meta-core/meta-restricted
- Add meta-restricted layer into “meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/bblayers.conf.sample” 

    BBLAYERS ?= " \
    :
    ##OEROOT##/meta-core/meta-bhs \
    ##OEROOT##/meta-core/meta-intel \
    ##OEROOT##/meta-core/meta-restricted \  <== Added
    :
- Enable Packages for Intel PFR

    Step 1 Enable PFR 
        Enable Intel PFR Support 
            Add IMAGE_FSTYPES += "intel-pfr" in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample
    
    Step 2 BHS Only, Enable 128MB vs 256MB BMC SPI Support 
        For 256MB BMC SPI support: 
            Add PFR_CONFIG = “pfr-256” in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample
        For 128MB BMC SPI support:
            Add PFR_CONFIG = “pfr-128” in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample

    For additional details (flashing, provisioning, usage), please refer to user’s guide. (MegaRAC OneTree™ - PFR Expansion Pack UserGuide )
```
###### Ami PFR Expansion Pack Configuration
```
- git clone https://git.ami.com/core/ami-bmc/one-tree/ami/amipacks/pfr/ami-pfr meta-ami-pfr
- Add meta-ami-pfr layer into “meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/bblayers.conf.sample” 

    BBLAYERS ?= " \
    :
    ##OEROOT##/meta-core/meta-bhs \
    ##OEROOT##/meta-core/meta-intel \
    ##OEROOT##/meta-ami-pfr \  <== Added
    :
- Ami-pfr layer should have higher priority than other layers
    for example:
            BBFILE_PRIORITY_meta-ami-pfr = "18" in meta-ami-pfr/conf/layer.conf 
            
    AMI-PFR is currently validated for the 2600 and 2700_evb_dcscm machines.
```

###### GPGPU Management Expansion Pack Configuration
```
- git clone https://git.ami.com/core/ami-bmc/one-tree/ami/amipacks/gp-gpu/nvidia-gpgpu/recipes-gpgpu  meta-ami/recipes-gpgpu

  Configure GPU support: enable Embedded GPU or Discrete GPGPU support depending on the platform.

- Embedded GPU Enablement (only for NVIDIA-platforms)

  Step#1 Enable Packages for GPGPU

    Add EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES:append = " onetree-gpgpu" in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample

  Step#2 Add GPU_SUPPORT_TYPE in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample or {BUILDDIR}/conf/local.conf
    
    # For GPU that support SMBPBI add below line
    GPU_SUPPORT_TYPE = "EMBEDDED_GPU_SMBPBI"

        # - The GPGPU EP has the support to auto-configure SMBPBI for the following GPU models: H100, H200, L40S, RTX_PRO_6000.

        # example: GPU_DEVICE_MODEL = "H100"
        GPU_DEVICE_SMBPBI_MODEL  = ""     
     
        # example: GPU_DEVICE_COUNT = "2"
        GPU_DEVICE_COUNT         = "" 
        
        # - The below variables must be SPACE-SEPARATED when specifying multiple GPUs
        # - Recommended format is HEX for bus IDs and addresses

        # example: "0x01 0x02" [usage: "<gpu1_i2c_bus_num> ... <gpuN_i2c_bus_num>" ]
        GPU_I2C_BUS_NUM          = ""           
 
        # example: "0x4c 0x4c" [usage: "<gpu1_slave_addr> ... <gpuN_slave_addr>" ]
        GPU_I2C_ADDRESS          = ""            
 
    [OR]

    # For GPU that supports NSM add below line
    GPU_SUPPORT_TYPE = "EMBEDDED_GPU_NSM"

    [OR]

    # For GPU that supports NSM_DBUS_SENSOR (OpenBmc) add below line
    GPU_SUPPORT_TYPE = "EMBEDDED_GPU_NSM_DBUS_SENSOR"
    
  Step#3 Add the gpgp-ep-config.inc in the conf/local.conf or machine conf file

    require ${AMIBASE}/recipes-gpgpu/recipe_classes/gpgpu-ep-config.inc in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample or {BUILDDIR}/conf/local.conf


- Discrete GPGPU Support (SMBPBI/NSM) (For NVIDIA/Non-NVIDIA platforms)

  Step#1 Clone the discrete-gpu layer

    git clone -b develop https://git.ami.com/core/ami-bmc/one-tree/ami/gp-gpu/nvidia-gpgpu/discrete-gpu.git meta-ami/recipes-gpgpu/discrete-gpu

  Step#2 Add the discrete GPU sub-layer to build/conf/bblayers.conf

    BBLAYERS ?= " \
        ... \
        </path/to/onetree/repo>/meta-ami/recipes-gpgpu/discrete-gpu \
        "

  Step#3 Enable the GPGPU feature in build/conf/local.conf

    EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES:append = " onetree-gpgpu"

  Step#4 Configure Discrete GPU Support - (DISCRETE_GPU_SMBPBI or DISCRETE_GPU_NSM)

    DISCRETE_GPU_SMBPBI - uses the SMBPBI protocol to communicate with supported NVIDIA GPUs. This protocol relies on the I2C bus for communication, so you will need to provide the I2C bus numbers and slave addresses for each GPU in your system.
    
    Supported SMBPBI models: H100, H100_NVL, H200, L4, L40, L40S, RTX_4000_ADA, RTX_PRO_4500_ServerEdition, RTX_PRO_4500_WorkStation, RTX_PRO_6000, RTX_PRO_6000_MAXQ

    Add the following configuration to {BUILDDIR}/conf/local.conf:

        GPU_SUPPORT_TYPE        = "DISCRETE_GPU_SMBPBI"
        GPU_COMM_PROTOCOL       = "SMBPBI"

        # Required: exact model string from the supported list above
        # example: GPU_DEVICE_SMBPBI_MODEL = "L40S"
        GPU_DEVICE_SMBPBI_MODEL = ""        

        # Number of GPUs in the system
        # example: GPU_DEVICE_COUNT        = "1"
        GPU_DEVICE_COUNT        = ""

        # I2C bus numbers: space-separated for multiple GPUs (hex recommended)
        # example: GPU_I2C_BUS_NUM = "0x01"
        GPU_I2C_BUS_NUM         = ""        

        # I2C slave addresses: order must match GPU_I2C_BUS_NUM
        # example: GPU_I2C_ADDRESS = "0x4c"
        GPU_I2C_ADDRESS         = "" 

    Note:For multi-GPU SMBPBI setups, the values in GPU_I2C_BUS_NUM and GPU_I2C_ADDRESS must be listed in the same order.

    [OR]

    DISCRETE_GPU_NSM - uses the NSM protocol to communicate with supported NVIDIA GPUs. This protocol relies on MCTP over USB for communication, so you will need to provide the NSM endpoint IDs (EIDs) for each GPU in your system.
    Supported NSM models: B200, B300, RTX_PRO_6000

    Add the following configuration to {BUILDDIR}/conf/local.conf:

       GPU_SUPPORT_TYPE     = "DISCRETE_GPU_NSM"
       GPU_COMM_PROTOCOL    = "NSM"

       # Required: exact model string from the supported list above
       # example: GPU_DEVICE_NSM_MODEL = "RTX_PRO_6000"
       GPU_DEVICE_NSM_MODEL = ""      

       # Number of GPUs in the system
       # example: GPU_DEVICE_COUNT        = "1"
       GPU_DEVICE_COUNT     = ""

       # NSM endpoint IDs (EIDs): space-separated for multiple GPUs
       # Currently the supported ID type is MCTP EID . This may be extended in the future to support other ID types such as UUID.
       ID_TYPE 	     = "eid" 

       # example: GPU_NSM_IDS = "13"
       GPU_NSM_IDS          = ""  

    Note:For NSM mode, provide one EID per GPU in GPU_NSM_IDS. 

```

###### Firmware Update Expansion Pack Configuration
```
- git clone https://git.ami.com/core/ami-bmc/one-tree/ami/amipacks/firmware-update.git meta-ami/meta-common/recipes-fwupdate
- Enable Packages for NON PFR Firmware Update
    a.  Enable CPLD Non PFR Update 
        OneTree™ provides mechanism to support CPLD firmware upgrade via jtag/spi/i2c interface. This feature will populate the CPLD Inventory and provide user mechanism to update the cpld using redfish update service. 

        Step 1: Comment out intel-pfr from IMAGE_FSTYPES in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample:
            # PFR image Build 
            #IMAGE_FSTYPES += "intel-pfr"

        Step 2: Enable CPLD
            Add EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES:append = " onetree-fwupdate onetree-fwupdate-cpld-update" in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample

    b.  Enable Signing Support 
        OneTree™ provides feature and mechanism that can be utilized to implement secure firmware updates and image verification. Before deploying firmware or software updates, you can sign the images using a cryptographic algorithm like RSA or ECC. This ensures that the images can be verified for authenticity and integrity during the update process. 

        Add EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES:append = " onetree-image-sign" in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample

    c.  Enable Dual Image Support  
        OneTree™ allows you to maintain two separate firmware images, commonly referred to as the primary and secondary images. One of these images is designated as the active image, while the other serves as a backup. OneTree™ can install the updated firmware into the bkup image slot while the active image remains untouched.

        Add EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES:append = " onetree-dual-image" in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample

        Enable Hardware fails safe, single spi abr support, sync conf 

        Add EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES:append = " onetree-hw-failsafe-boot" in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample
        Add EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES:append = " onetree-single-spi-abr" in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample
        Add EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES:append = " onetree-sync-conf" in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample
```

###### AMD Remote Debug Expansion Pack Configuration
```
Chalupa
- git clone https://git.ami.com/core/ami-bmc/one-tree/amd/amdpacks/remote-debug meta-amd/meta-chalupa/recipes-amd/amd-remote-debug
Venice
- git clone https://git.ami.com/core/ami-bmc/one-tree/amd/amdpacks/remote-debug.git meta-amd/meta-venice/recipes-amd/amd-remote-debug
- Enable Packages for AMD Remote Debug

    Add EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES:append = "amd-remote-debug" in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample
```

###### NIC Expansion Pack Configuration
```
- git clone https://git.ami.com/core/ami-bmc/one-tree/ami/amipacks/nic meta-ami/recipes-ami/nic
- Enable Packages for NIC

    Add EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES:append = " onetree-nic" in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample
```

###### NVMe Expansion Pack Configuration
```
- git clone https://git.ami.com/core/ami-bmc/one-tree/ami/amipacks/nvme meta-ami/recipes-ami/nvme 
- Enable Packages for NVMe. Only one of onetree-nvme and onetree-nvmebasic can be enabled at a time

    a. Enable NVMe Management 
        Add EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES:append = " onetree-nvme" in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample
    b. Enable NVMe Basic Management 
        Add EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES:append = " onetree-nvmebasic" in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample
```

###### BRCM Pcie Switch Expansion Pack Configuration
```
- git clone https://git.ami.com/core/ami-bmc/one-tree/ami/amipacks/pciesw-brcm.git meta-ami/recipes-ami/pciesw-brcm
- Enable Packages for PCIe Switch
    a. Enable Pcie Switch I2C Pciesw 
        Add IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " i2c-pciesw " in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample
    b. Enable Pcie Switch Libscrutiny 
        Add IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " libscrutiny " in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample
    c. Enable Pcie Switch BRCM MCTP 
        Add IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " mctp-pciesw " in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample
    d. Enable Pcie Switch Pciesw Service Interface 
        Add IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " pciesw-service " in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample
    e. Enable Pcie Switch Scrutiny Service Interface 
        Add IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " scrutiny-ifc " in meta-core/META-XXX/conf/templates/default/local.conf.sample
```


### Notes
- Package groups will be used for features and expansion pack configuration, also build script will be given to simplify the build process from OneTree2.1
- By default root user is disabled in the stack except AST2600EVB
- uncomment EXTRA_IMAGE_FEATURES += "debug-tweaks" in build/conf/local.conf to enable the root user access

